-- Step 27: supplier returns (debit notes).
-- track: B
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / index statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/*/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed by Drizzle.
-- Reverse with the file of the same name in drizzle/down.
--
-- Goods sent back to a supplier are written against one posted goods received note. Each line
-- sends back so much of one of its lines: either of what no bill has billed yet, or of what one
-- posted bill billed. The return is a draft the app writes. Posting it is one act of the
-- database, app.post_supplier_return. The goods leave the warehouse at what the stock is
-- carried at that day (the weighted average, as every move out), and:
--
--   debit   Goods received not invoiced   goods not billed: what they came into stock at
--   debit   Trade payables                goods billed: what the bill charged for them, with
--                                         its sales tax (a debit note: the supplier owes it back)
--   credit  Sales tax receivable          the input tax claimed on those billed goods
--   credit  Stock in trade                what the goods left stock at
--   debit   or credit  Purchase price differences   whatever is left between the two
--
-- What the supplier owes back for billed goods comes off the bill the goods were billed on, as
-- far as that bill is still owed; the rest stays a credit with the supplier, set against other
-- bills of the same supplier later with app.apply_supplier_return_credit. Nothing reaches the
-- books with that: both sides are what is owed to the same supplier.
--
-- Tax that was withheld on the bill is not given back by a return: it was the supplier's tax,
-- paid over or to be paid over on its behalf, and the supplier owes the whole value back.
--
-- Goods sent back unbilled can no longer be billed: app.post_supplier_bill (Step 25, this
-- track's) is written out again below to count them, and app.bill_owed (Step 26, this track's)
-- to count what returns have taken off a bill.
--
-- The owner and an accountant write and post returns; the auditor reads them. The app's role
-- cannot write a return's status, number, journal or figures, nor what its credit was set
-- against.
--
-- Database error codes of this track are SE200 to SE299 (docs/PARALLEL.md); Step 30 used SE200
-- to SE210, Step 24 SE211 to SE222, Step 25 SE223 to SE234 and Step 26 SE235 to SE245:
--   SE246  no such supplier return in this company (or outside the member's branches)
--   SE247  the return is not in the state this needs
--   SE248  a posted return, and what its credit was set against, is never changed or removed
--   SE249  a line is written only while its return is a draft; it is a line of the return's
--          goods received note and, where it names a bill line, of a posted bill of the same
--          supplier for those goods
--   SE250  a return is posted with at least one line
--   SE251  more sent back than was received and is left: not yet billed, or billed on that bill
--   SE252  a date that has not come yet, is no day on the calendar, or is before the goods
--          were received or billed
--   SE253  a return's credit is set against posted bills of its supplier and branch, each for
--          no more than is owed on it, in all for no more than is left of the credit
--   SE254  a return follows its goods received note: its supplier, its warehouse, that
--          warehouse's branch
-- SE219 (purchase documents are written in read committed transactions) is Step 24's, used
-- again; SE060 (not enough in stock) is the stock function's.

